course: dictionary
lesson: 13466
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word hurdles is a good example. «The runners leapt over the hurdles at sports day.» Here the hurdles are the frames you jump over in a race.
explain: «She cleared her first hurdle when she passed the spelling test.» Nobody is jumping anything here. A hurdle can also be a problem you must get past, and the clue is that she passed a test. Ask: does this meaning fit the sentence? If not, try another one.
explain: Hurdle can also be a verb. «He hurdled the gate and ran off across the field.» Hurdled means jumped over something while running. The same word can be a noun in one sentence and a verb in the next, so look at how it is used.
fact: Hurdles (noun) means a race in which runners jump over a row of light frames, such as the 100 metres hurdles.
fact: A hurdle is also a problem or difficulty you must get past, as in «the last hurdle before the holidays».
fact: Long ago, a hurdle was a movable fence panel of woven sticks, used to pen sheep.
fact: Hurdle (verb) means to jump over something while running; hurdles, hurdled and hurdling are its other forms.
fact: A good check is to put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The runners raced over the hurdles.» What are the hurdles in this sentence? | Pens for sheep with gates | A set of tall trees | *A row of light frames to jump over | Long, wet grass
exercise: «Our team cleared the last hurdle and won the cup.» What does hurdle mean here? | A sports prize | *A problem or difficulty you must get past | A fence made of woven sticks | A race for dogs
exercise: «The farmer built a pen from wooden hurdles.» What is a hurdle in this sentence? | A running race | A tall tree | *A movable fence panel of woven sticks | A difficult problem
test: «Ruby hurdled the puddle on her way to school.» What does hurdled mean? | Walked carefully around | *Jumped over while running | Splashed through slowly | Fell into
test: In «I can hurdle that fence», what kind of word is hurdle? | Noun | Adjective | *Verb | Adverb
exam: In «Jamal trained hard for the hurdles, but long division is his next hurdle», what does hurdle mean in the second part? | *A problem you must get past | A wooden fence for sheep | To run very fast | A frame you jump over in a race
